+
+## Sales and variance
+
+`POST /import/sales` accepts a JSON object with a `csv` string. Supply the
+columns `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`, a timezone-qualified ISO instant and a
+positive whole number of portions. A ticket may span multiple rows. Previously
+imported tickets are skipped. The response counts new distinct tickets and
+total portions in `{ "tickets": 1, "dishes": 3 }`. Invalid rows and shortages
+identify the source row and discard the whole import.
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array in item
+ID order for the inclusive UTC date range. Each row contains `itemId`,
+`theoretical` (ingredients required by sales), `actual` (all consumption),
+and `variance` (actual minus theoretical), in the item's unit.
